      {
        "ruleId": "vue/require-v-for-key",
        "ruleDocsPath": "docs/content/rules/vue.md",
        "severity": 2,
        "message": "[vize:vue/require-v-for-key] Elements in iteration expect to have 'v-bind:key' directives. Element: <div>",
        "line": 14,
        "column": 4,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endColumn": 69,
        "help": "Why: The :key attribute helps Vue's virtual DOM efficiently track and update list items.\nFix: Add a unique identifier as the key:\n  <li v-for=\"item in items\" :key=\"item.id\">\n  {{ item.name }}\n  </li>\nBest practices:\n- Use unique, stable identifiers (like database IDs)\n- Avoid using array index as key when list order may change\n- Keys must be primitive values (string or number)"
      },
      {
        "ruleId": "vue/permitted-contents",
        "ruleDocsPath": "docs/content/rules/vue.md",
        "severity": 2,
        "message": "[vize:vue/permitted-contents] <div> is not phrasing content, but <span> only permits phrasing content",
        "line": 56,
        "column": 7,
        "endLine": 56,
        "endColumn": 11,
        "help": "Why: the HTML standard's content models define which elements may contain which. The browser builds this DOM as written, but the document is non-conforming: assistive technology, validators and future parsers may treat it differently.\nFix: use an element the parent permits (phrasing content such as <span> inside <p>/<span>, <li> inside lists), or restructure so interactive elements are not nested."
      }
    ],
    "errorCount": 2,
    "warningCount": 1
  },
